b12x 1.5.1: apply swiglu_limit in the W4A8-MX tiny-decode MoE path (T <= 4)

Bug (FlashInfer issue #6866 / b12x): fused_moe w4a8_mx with n % 128 == 0 routes
1..4 tokens to kernels/tiny_decode.py, whose FC2 computes silu(gate) * up without
the SwiGLU clamp. _launch_micro never forwards swiglu_limit to it, so models with
a clamp (DeepSeek V4.1: swiglu_limit 10) get unclamped expert outputs in decode.
The dynamic and compact-micro paths clamp correctly.

Fix: the tiny-decode kernel takes swiglu_limit as a compile-time constant (part of
the kernel cache key) and clamps like nvfp4_phase1._activated_value / the
reference: gate = min(gate, L), up = clamp(up, -L, L), then silu(gate) * up * w.
Without a limit the generated code is unchanged. The custom op
b12x::tp_moe_tiny_decode_launch gets a `float? swiglu_limit` argument, and the
preparation prewarm resolves the same (clamped) kernel. tiny_decode.py exports
SWIGLU_LIMIT_SUPPORTED = True, which sm120/sm120_patches.py detects.

Apply (inside the image, after `pip install b12x==1.5.1`):
  SITE=$(python3 -c 'import b12x, os; print(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(b12x.__file__)))')
  patch -p1 -d "$SITE" < b12x-tiny-decode-swiglu.patch
Test: python3 test_b12x_tiny_decode_swiglu.py

